# ATTRACT MODE -- our own block (Part 01, section 1.9, item 6).
#
# Pulled into the live configuration by ONE line at the end of
# hosting/Caddyfile:
#     import ../attract-mode/hosting/attract-mode.caddy
# Caddy reads import paths relative to the Caddyfile's own folder, so the
# path starts with ".." on purpose.
#
# THE PORTS ARE THE BIBLE'S, NOT OURS (Part 01, 1.4 and Part 11, 11.5):
#   8081  everything www.strulovitz.org serves today, and pre.strulovitz.org
#   8082  learnime.com
#   8083  peaktogether.me
#   8084  Attract Mode: Moodle plus our plain files, from Switch Day
#
# SO "pre" NEEDS NOTHING HERE. pre.strulovitz.org is the tunnel's job: its
# entry points at 127.0.0.1:8081, the old site's own port (Nir's owner act
# O2). An earlier version of this file wrongly listened on 8084 and gave
# that port to "pre"; 8084 belongs to Moodle. Corrected 2026-11-28.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE HOLDS NOW: the 8084 door, reserved and answering plainly,
# so the port is declared in the configuration before Stage 2 needs it.
# Nothing on the public internet points here yet.
#
# AT STAGE 2 this block is replaced by the real thing (Part 08, section
# 8.5): Caddy answers /am/ itself, everything else goes to Moodle's public
# folder with PHP running as Nir's own user, and anything that matches no
# file goes to Moodle's router.

:8084 {
	bind 127.0.0.1
	respond "Attract Mode is being built. Nothing is for sale yet." 200
}
